    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_culture_identity_concession_rebuttal",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-culture-identity-01",
        "slug": "c1-culture-identity-concession-rebuttal",
        "title": "Concession followed by rebuttal",
        "rule_summary": "Acknowledge a reasonable opposing point before limiting it or presenting a stronger counterargument.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "ابتدا یک نکته منطقی از طرف مقابل را می‌پذیریم و سپس دامنه آن را محدود می‌کنیم یا پاسخ قوی‌تری می‌دهیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "Granted, the process is faster; that does not necessarily make it fairer.",
            "fa": "درست است که روند سریع‌تر است؛ اما لزوماً عادلانه‌تر نیست."
          },
          {
            "en": "While that concern is valid, it overlooks the cost of doing nothing.",
            "fa": "با اینکه آن نگرانی معتبر است، هزینه هیچ کاری نکردن را نادیده می‌گیرد."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_culture_identity_advanced_hedging",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-culture-identity-02",
        "slug": "c1-culture-identity-advanced-hedging",
        "title": "Advanced hedging and calibration",
        "rule_summary": "Calibrate certainty with expressions such as arguably, broadly speaking, tends to, appears to, and cannot entirely be ruled out.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "در C1 میزان قطعیت را با عبارت‌هایی مثل arguably، broadly speaking، tends to، appears to و cannot entirely be ruled out دقیق تنظیم می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "The change appears to have improved access, although the evidence is still limited.",
            "fa": "به نظر می‌رسد این تغییر دسترسی را بهتر کرده، هرچند شواهد هنوز محدود است."
          },
          {
            "en": "That explanation cannot entirely be ruled out.",
            "fa": "نمی‌توان آن توضیح را کاملاً منتفی دانست."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_culture_identity_reduced_relatives",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-culture-identity-03",
        "slug": "c1-culture-identity-reduced-relatives",
        "title": "Reduced relative clauses",
        "rule_summary": "Reduce relative clauses when the meaning remains clear, especially in formal descriptions and summaries.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "در توصیف‌ها و خلاصه‌های رسمی، وقتی معنا روشن می‌ماند relative clause را کوتاه می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "The measures introduced last year are being reviewed.",
            "fa": "اقداماتی که پارسال معرفی شدند در حال بازبینی‌اند."
          },
          {
            "en": "People working remotely reported fewer interruptions.",
            "fa": "افرادی که دورکاری می‌کردند مزاحمت کمتری گزارش کردند."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "external_id": "d_c1_culture_identity_scene_1",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-culture-identity-01",
        "title": "Culture & Identity: part 1",
        "setting": "seminar break",
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "likes-dislikes",
        "characters": [
          "Mei",
          "Omar"
        ],
        "turns": [
          {
            "order": 1,
            "speaker": "Mei",
            "text": "Which assumption is doing most of the work here?",
            "translation_fa": "کدوم فرض بیشترین نقش رو در این استدلال داره؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 2,
            "speaker": "Omar",
            "text": "Identity is rarely a single category; people may emphasize different parts of it in different contexts without being inconsistent.",
            "translation_fa": "هویت به‌ندرت فقط یک دسته‌ست؛ آدم‌ها ممکنه در زمینه‌های مختلف بخش‌های متفاوتش رو برجسته کنن بدون اینکه متناقض باشن."
          },
          {
            "order": 3,
            "speaker": "Mei",
            "text": "How would the conclusion change if that assumption failed?",
            "translation_fa": "اگر اون فرض برقرار نباشه نتیجه چطور عوض می‌شه؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 4,
            "speaker": "Omar",
            "text": "A sense of belonging can come from language, place, relationships, shared experience, or several of these at once.",
